[?2004h> """Read one station's raw daily file and turn it into the standard daily inputs used by ``fao56.et0_daily``.
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +The raw files use the column names described in ``/app/docs/METHOD.md``.  This module converts those raw
[?2004l[?2004h> +measurements into the *standard* units expected by the FAO‑56 implementation:
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +* Temperatures are already provided in °C.
[?2004l[?2004h> +* Relative humidity or dew‑point is converted to actual vapour pressure (kPa) using the helper functions
[?2004l[?2004h> +  in :pymod:`et0.fao56`.
[?2004l[?2004h> +* Wind speed may be measured at an anemometer height other than 2 m.  When ``station.wind_height_m`` differs
[?2004l[?2004h> +  from 2 m, the FAO‑56 wind‑speed adjustment (Eq. 47) is applied:
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +  ``u2 = u_z * (4.87 / log(67.8*z - 5.42))``
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +  where ``z`` is the measurement height in metres.
[?2004l[?2004h> +* Solar radiation can be supplied either in MJ m⁻² day⁻¹ (the standard) or in W m⁻².  When the latter is used we
[?2004l[?2004h> +  convert to MJ m⁻² day⁻¹ by multiplying by 0.0864 (1 W m⁻² sustained for a day = 86 400 J m⁻² = 0.0864 MJ m⁻²).
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +These conversions make the pipeline robust for *any* station register that follows the formats described in the
[?2004l[?2004h> +method document.
[?2004l[?2004h> +"""
[?2004l[?2004h> +
