[?2004l[?2004h> """Read one station's raw daily file and turn it into the standard daily inputs used by ``fao56.et0_daily``.
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +The raw files use the column names described in ``/app/docs/METHOD.md``.  This module converts those raw
[?2004l[?2004h> +measurements into the *standard* units expected by the FAO‑56 implementation:
[?2004l[?2004h> +
[?2004l[?2004h> +* Temperatures are already provided in °C.
[?2004l[?2004h> +* Relative humidity or dew‑point is converted to actual vapour pressure (kPa) using the helper functions
[?2004l[?2004h> +  in :pymod:`et0.fao56`.
[?2004l[?2004h> +* Wind speed may be measured at an anemometer height other than 2 m.  When ``station.wind_height_m`` differs
[?2004l[?2004h> +  from 2 m, the FAO‑56 wind‑speed adjustment (Eq. 47) is applied:
[?2004l[?2004h> +
